Scratch: forever
Arduino: void loop() { }
Runs again and again, top to bottom, until you unplug it.

Scratch: when green flag clicked
Arduino: void setup() { }
Runs ONE time, at the very start.

Scratch: wait 1 seconds
Arduino: delay(1000);
1000 = one second's worth of milliseconds.

digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
delay(1000);
One finished instruction = one semicolon.

void loop() {
   these lines belong to loop
}

pinMode(13, OUTPUT);
"Pin 13, your job is to send."
In setup() — so it runs ONCE.
